I just switched to a new computer with Windows 2000, and had trouble
getting the DOS screen looking right; it was all vertically squished.
(I've since found the solution, thanks to DejaGoogle and rgrn.)  So I
tried using the graphical interface, which led to me whacking at a
number of things that I wouldn't normally whack at, including nymphs
and floating eyes.

After a few fruitless games, I started yet another incarnation of
Snake the Neutral Healer.  This time she found several wands in the
first three levels, and by the time she reached level four, she
decided it was time to try to engrave-ID them.  Since there were two
glass wands in her stash, she was pretty sure those were wands of
light, but she went through the proper motions.  Instead, "You may
wish for an object."  Two blessed scrolls of charging and GDSM,
please!  Alas, the armor was +0 instead of +2, but still a big
improvement over the spiked leather armor she'd been wearing.

Flushed with success (or hubris), she went down to the Gnomish Mines
to try her luck.  Alas, she whacked a small icon that turned out to be
a nymph.  The nymph promptly stole her scalpel, her GDSM, and one of
the wands of wishing, leaving her almost defenseless.  (None of the
other wands turned out to be useful offensively.)

She retreated back to the main dungeon to regroup.  One wand of
wishing left, so at least four potential wishes.  But she really
didn't want to use wishes too profligately; it was inelegant.  So
after a bit of thought, she wished for a wand of death.  If the bounce
killed her, so be it.

Armed with the /oD, she went back to the Gnomish Mines to hunt some
nymph.  The first time she spotted the damned nymph, she spent too
much time lining up her shot and the nymph got away with her knife
that had replaced the scalpel.  But the second shot got her, and it
was the right nymph.  GDSM, scalpel, /oW, and three potions of healing
recovered, she went on down, hoping to avoid any more acquisitive
nymphs.

The next level was lit, which was nice.  The first thing she saw was a
purple "h" around three squares away.  Probably a dwarf king, given
the location, but better check.  Oops, not a dwarf king -- a master
mind flayer.  Out came the /oD again, and the mmf was no fun at all;
he fell right over.

The next level was Gnometown, where there were two lamps in the
hardware store.  One was 8 gold, but the other was 38 gold.

So now Snake the Healer has a practically unlimited stock of wishes,
plus a permanent source of light.  No doubt something stupid will kill
her soon.

How will she die?


